    {
      "id": "be-s8-cost-concepts-c4",
      "heading": "Reading costs as areas on the graph",
      "explanation_md": "At an output Q0 each cost is a **rectangle**:\n\n- **Fixed cost** = Q0 x (ATC - AVC) = Q0 x AFC = FC\n- **Variable cost** = Q0 x AVC = VC(Q0)\n- **Total cost** = Q0 x ATC = C(Q0)\n\nThe gap between ATC and AVC is AFC, which is why it shrinks as Q grows.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
