      "stem": "What is a sunk cost, and why should managers ignore it?",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "A **sunk cost** is a cost that is **forever lost** after it has been paid. Managers should **ignore** it when deciding, because no future choice can recover it; only costs that change with the decision matter for maximising profit or minimising losses.",
